[
  {
    "id": "p1",
    "text": "Before running the full suite in a fresh checkout, run `./tools/gen-fixtures --seed 8cb1d00d4806` (the team seed). It writes the gitignored `.fixtures/golden.json`, and `tests/test_ledger.py` fails at import without it.",
    "helpful": 4,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p2",
    "text": "Run the whole test suite with `tools/test`. It sets `PYTHONPATH=src` for the src layout. Running `python3 -m unittest` directly without that can fail to import `tally`.",
    "helpful": 4,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p3",
    "text": "Every change needs a one-line entry under `## Unreleased` at the top of CHANGELOG.md (format: \"- `command --flag` does X.\"). Add it in the same change as the code and tests.",
    "helpful": 3,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p4",
    "text": "For CLI tests in tests/test_cli.py, argparse rejections (bad `type=` values, missing required flags) raise SystemExit, not a return code. Assert them with `with self.assertRaises(SystemExit) as cm:` and check `cm.exception.code == 2`. `run()` does not return these.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p5",
    "text": "Money splitting convention (`money.split`): the parts must sum exactly to the amount, differ by at most one cent, and any extra cents go to the first parts. Test with `money.split(Decimal('100.00'), 3)` == `[33.34, 33.33, 33.33]`.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  }
]
